Here is the problem description:
<description>
Vanya has a scales for weighing loads and weights of masses w0, w1, w2, ..., w100 grams where w is some integer not less than 2 (exactly one weight of each nominal value). Vanya wonders whether he can weight an item with mass m using the given weights, if the weights can be put on both pans of the scales. Formally speaking, your task is to determine whether it is possible to place an item of mass m and some weights on the left pan of the scales, and some weights on the right pan of the scales so that the pans of the scales were in balance.
</description>

Here is the input specification:
<input_spec>
The first line contains two integers w, m (2 ≤ w ≤ 109, 1 ≤ m ≤ 109) — the number defining the masses of the weights and the mass of the item.
</input_spec>

Here are additional notes:
<notes>
NoteNote to the first sample test. One pan can have an item of mass 7 and a weight of mass 3, and the second pan can have two weights of masses 9 and 1, correspondingly. Then 7 + 3 = 9 + 1.Note to the second sample test. One pan of the scales can have an item of mass 99 and the weight of mass 1, and the second pan can have the weight of mass 100.Note to the third sample test. It is impossible to measure the weight of the item in the manner described in the input. 
</notes>

Here are sample inputs:
<sample_inputs>
<input>
3 7
</input>
<input>
100 99
</input>
<input>
100 50
</input>
</sample_inputs>

Here is the source code:
<source_code>
import java.math.BigInteger;
import java.util.Scanner;


public class Main {

    private static int weight;
    private static int itemMass;
    private static boolean[] arr=new boolean[100];
    static{
        for(int i=0;i<100;i++)
            arr[i]=false;
    }
    public boolean isBalanced(){
        boolean isBalance=false;
        long pod1=itemMass, pod2=0;

        while(true){
            if(pod1>pod2){
                long nextMass=getMass(pod1-pod2);
                //System.out.println("Pod1 wieght is higher: "+nextMass);
                if(nextMass!=0){
                    pod2+=nextMass;
                }
                else
                    break;
            }
            else if(pod1<pod2){
                long nextMass1=getMass(pod2-pod1);
                //System.out.println("Pod2 wieght is higher: "+nextMass1);
                if(nextMass1!=0){
                    pod1+=nextMass1;
                }
                else
                    break;
            }
            else{
                isBalance=true;
                break;
            }
        }
        return isBalance;
    }

    public long getMass(long mass){
        long result;
        int logBase=(int) (Math.log(mass)/Math.log(weight));
        //System.out.println("Mass is "+mass+" log is: "+logBase);
        //long sumTotal=((long) Math.pow(weight, logBase+1)-1)/(weight-1);

        BigInteger bi=new BigInteger(Integer.toString(weight));
        //System.out.println(bi.toString());
        bi=bi.pow(logBase+1);
        //System.out.println(bi.toString());
        bi=bi.subtract(new BigInteger(Integer.toString(1)));
        //System.out.println(bi.toString());
        bi=bi.divide(new BigInteger(Integer.toString(weight-1)));
        //System.out.println(bi.toString());
        long sumTotal=bi.longValue();

        //System.out.println("Mass is "+mass+" log is: "+logBase+" total mass is: "+sumTotal+" arr value: "+arr[logBase+1]+" "+arr[logBase]);
        if(mass>sumTotal && !arr[logBase+1]){
            result=(int) Math.pow(weight, logBase+1);
            arr[logBase+1]=true;
        }
        else if(mass<=sumTotal && !arr[logBase]){
            result=(int) Math.pow(weight, logBase);
            arr[logBase]=true;
        }
        else{
            result=0;
        }

        return result;  
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // TODO Auto-generated method stub
        Scanner sc=new Scanner(System.in);
        Main.weight=sc.nextInt();
        Main.itemMass=sc.nextInt();
        Main wb=new Main();

        if(wb.isBalanced())
            System.out.println("YES");
        else
            System.out.println("NO");
    }

}

</source_code>
